# Clorox (CLX) Morningstar Deep Undervaluation Study

> Study date: May 19, 2026
> Morningstar Fair Value: $163 | Current Price: $92.82 | Potential Gain: +75.6%
> Moat Rating: Wide Moat | Industry: Home & Personal Care Products

---

## 1. Company Profile

### Main business

The Clorox Company, founded in 1913 and headquartered in Oakland, California, is a leading consumer products company in the United States. The company manufactures and sells products such as household cleaning, disinfecting, food, trash bags, cat litter, charcoal, water filtration and natural personal care.

### Revenue structure (four major business segments)

| Business segments | Main brands | Revenue proportion (approximately) |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| Health & Wellness | Clorox Bleach, Pine-Sol, Liquid-Plumr, Tilex | ~38% (~$2.7 billion) |
| Household | Glad trash bags, Kingsford charcoal, Fresh Step cat litter | ~28% |
| Lifestyle | Hidden Valley, Brita, Burt's Bees | ~18% |
| International | Overseas sales of the above brands | ~14% |

The U.S. market contributes approximately 86% of total revenue.

### Market position

- More than 80% of its U.S. sales come from the first or second category brands
- Leading positions in bleach, charcoal, garbage bags, salad dressings, multi-purpose cleaners, water filtration and other categories
- High brand household penetration and strong consumer loyalty

